Enhancement: Reduce memory usage when saving very large metadata blobs

Before uploading data, restic checks it once more for corruption. For very large
blobs, such as the metadata of a directory with hundreds of thousands of
entries, this check held a second full copy of the blob in memory, doubling
memory usage at that point.

Restic now performs this check for large blobs without the extra copy. What is
checked is unchanged.

